          "page": 3,
          "section": "2.1. Preparation of HfMoNbTaTi alloys",
          "quote": "The sintering procedure is illustrated in Fig. 1 (c) and comprised the following steps: (1) Heating-up stage: The combination body was heated up to the target sintering temperature at a heating rate of 50 °C/min. The sintering temperature was set to 1400 °C – 1700 °C at 50 °C intervals. Simultaneously, the sintering pressure was uniformly increased to 50 MPa. (2) Holding stage: The combination body was maintained at the sintering temperature and pressure for 15 min. (3) Furnace cooling stage: At the conclusion of the holding stage, the sintering pressure was rapidly decreased. The combination body was cooled to room temperature within the furnace.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": "Fig. 1(c)",
